From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 14:39:23 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] venus: pass through VK_KHR_pipeline_binary

The local venus-protocol series gives the extension's five commands their
command ids and codecs, and the renderer now tracks VkPipelineBinaryKHR as an
object, so the driver can carry the extension by forwarding each command and
naming the binaries it creates.

vkCreatePipelineBinariesKHR is the only command with work of its own. Its
count is in-out inside VkPipelineBinaryHandlesInfoKHR and an application asks
how many binaries a pipeline yields by offering no handle array, so a query
names no objects and creates none. When handles are offered, the driver names
one object per handle up front, because the renderer needs an id for each
binary before it can create one, and releases the objects the host driver did
not take once the reply says how many it filled. The renderer never saw those
ids, so releasing them crosses no ring.

vkReleaseCapturedPipelineDataKHR is submitted asynchronously. It returns no
data, its only failure is host allocation, and waiting for a reply would stall
the ring for a capture-tooling command.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
